      "id": "5fafaf52-60d5-4b27-ae90-4e11fd9047fc",
      "name": "[cred] Apify - verify the addresses"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Source and verify B2B leads with Apify into Google Sheets\n\n**Who's it for**\nB2B sales and lead-generation teams who want a repeatable pipeline from \"the kind of company I\nwant\" to a verified contact list with a drafted first email, all recorded in Google Sheets.\n\n**How it works**\nTwo passes that share one spreadsheet.\n\n**Sourcing** starts when you submit the search brief. Companies are sourced, split one per row and\nsaved. The batch is sent to an Apify actor that finds contact emails from LinkedIn, rows with no\nemail are dropped rather than carried forward, and what remains is passed to a second Apify actor\nthat verifies each address. Only verified contacts reach the final tab, so the list you work from\nhas already had the bounces taken out.\n\n**Outreach** is a separate pass you run when you are ready. It reads the verified leads and the log\nof what has already been sent, drops anyone previously contacted, and asks an AI agent - with an\nApify research tool available to it - to draft a first email per lead. The drafts are written back\nto the sheet for review rather than sent, so a human approves before anything leaves.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Attach Google Sheets credentials and point each sheet node at your spreadsheet and tab.\n2. Attach an Apify credential to the three Apify nodes and set your actor ids.\n3. Attach an OpenRouter credential to the model node.\n4. Submit the form once with a small search to watch a batch flow through end to end.\n\n**Requirements**\nAn Apify account with actors for company sourcing, LinkedIn email lookup and email verification, an\nOpenRouter API key, and a Google Sheet.\n\n**How to customize**\nThe tone and structure of the first email is the prompt on **`write the outreach email`**. To change\nwhat counts as a usable lead, edit **`drop rows with no email`**.",
        "height": 1126,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -1466
      ],
      "id": "sticky-00",
      "name": "Template overview"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Source the companies\n\nThe form carries the search brief. **`split the companies`** turns the response into one item per company so each is saved as its own row.\n\n**`collect the companies`** batches them back up, because the LinkedIn lookup is far cheaper called once with many companies than once per company.",
        "height": 224,
        "width": 1040,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        280,
        -264
      ],
      "id": "sticky-01",
      "name": "1. Source the companies"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Drop what you cannot use, early\n\n**`drop rows with no email`** removes contacts the lookup could not resolve.\n\nThis sits *before* verification on purpose: verification is charged per address, and paying to verify a blank is the easiest money to waste in a pipeline like this.",
        "height": 202,
        "width": 1040,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1400,
        480
      ],
      "id": "sticky-02",
      "name": "2. Drop what you cannot use"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Verify before it counts as a lead\n\nOnly addresses that pass verification reach the final tab.\n\nThat tab is what the outreach pass reads, so the bounces are taken out of the list before anyone writes to it - rather than discovered afterwards in a sending tool's bounce report.",
        "height": 268,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2520,
        -118
      ],
      "id": "sticky-03",
      "name": "3. Verify before it counts"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4. Never contact the same person twice\n\nThe outreach pass reads **both** the verified leads and the log of what has already gone out, then **`drop leads already contacted`** removes the overlap.\n\nThe log is the memory. Without it, re-running this pass would draft a fresh first email to everybody you already approached.",
        "height": 202,
        "width": 1320,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        280,
        750
      ],
      "id": "sticky-04",
      "name": "4. Never contact twice"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 5. Drafted, not sent\n\n**`write the outreach email`** has an Apify research tool available, so it can look something up about a company before writing rather than guessing from the row.\n\nThe drafts are written back to the sheet. **Nothing is sent from this workflow** - a human reads the column and approves, which is the right default for a first email to a stranger.",
        "height": 312,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1680,
        -352
      ],
      "id": "sticky-05",
      "name": "5. Drafted, not sent"
    }
  ],
